// Biome config extending Ultracite's presets - the optional React/Next starting
// point, not the default. The default TypeScript lint gate is raw oxlint with
// references/typescript-oxlintrc.jsonc plus oxfmt; Ultracite's traps and the
// case for demoting it are in references/typescript.md, "Lint families and suppressions".
//
// WHAT IT GATES: Biome's own rule set on top of Ultracite core/react/next, the
// vitest test-hygiene rules, and the formatter. Every override below states what
// breaks without it; add none without the same.
//
// HOW TO WIRE IT:
//   pnpm add -D @biomejs/biome ultracite
//   pnpm exec biome check src tests          # lint + format + assists
//   pnpm exec biome lint --error-on-warnings src tests
// Verified 2026-09-03 against biome 2.5.11 and ultracite 7.10.7: this file as
// shipped exits 1 on a test file carrying `test.only`, `test.skip` and an
// assertion-free test (3 lint diagnostics), and 0 on a clean file.
//
// TRAPS:
//  - THE EXTENSION IS LOAD-BEARING. Biome silently discards a `biome.json` that
//    holds `//` comments - the whole file, `extends` chain included - and falls
//    back to defaults. Measured on the identical content: as `biome.json`,
//    `biome lint` on the three-violation test file reports 1 warning and EXITS
//    0; as `biome.jsonc`, 3 errors and exit 1. Keep the name `biome.jsonc`.
//  - IT NEEDS AN IGNORE FILE. With no `.gitignore`, `.git/info/exclude` or
//    `.ignore` in the folder holding this config, Biome reports
//    `internalError/fs ... couldn't find an ignore file` and exits 1 with zero
//    lint output - a config error dressed as a gate failure. A 0-byte
//    `.gitignore` does NOT satisfy it (verified: same error); one line of
//    content does. `git init` alone is enough, because it writes
//    `.git/info/exclude`, so the case that bites inside a healthy repo is a
//    monorepo package linted from its own cwd.
//  - THE `$schema` PIN DRIFTS IN SILENCE. Pinning 2.5.1 or even 2.0.0 against
//    CLI 2.5.11 produces no diagnostic here and no exit-code change; it only
//    costs editor completion. Bump it with `biome migrate --write`, and read
//    that command's diff before applying: it rewrites a pretty-printed
//    `rules: { recommended: true }` to `preset: "none"`, which switches the
//    linter off while still exiting 0.
//  - NURSERY RULES CANNOT BE ENABLED FROM `overrides[]`. `useExpect` below is
//    nursery and has to sit in the top-level `linter.rules`.
//  - SEVERITY MUST BE THE LITERAL `"error"`. `"on"` keeps a rule's default
//    severity, so a rule that visibly reads as enabled still does not gate; and
//    `--error-on-warnings` lifts warnings only, never the info tier.
//  - Ultracite's core hard-excludes any directory named `dist`, `build`, `out`,
//    `.next` and similar with `!!` globs this file cannot re-include. A gate
//    pointed at such a path exits 1 with `Checked 0 files`.
//  - A misspelled rule key fails closed (`Found an unknown key`, exit 1, nothing
//    linted), so config typos are loud. Path globs are the quiet half.
{
  "$schema": "https://biomejs.dev/schemas/2.5.11/schema.json",
  "extends": [
    "ultracite/biome/core",
    "ultracite/biome/react",
    "ultracite/biome/next",
    // The test-hygiene rules (noFocusedTests, noSkippedTests, noExportsInTest,
    // noMisplacedAssertion and the rest) at error severity. Without this entry
    // a committed `test.only` passes the gate: see references/typescript-
    // testing.md, "Test lint rules".
    "ultracite/biome/vitest"
  ],
  "files": {
    // Project-local exclusions only. The build-output and cache directories are
    // already excluded by ultracite/biome/core.
    "includes": ["**", "!**/*.generated.*", "!pnpm-lock.yaml"]
  },
  "linter": {
    "rules": {
      "correctness": {
        // Tailwind's `theme()` in CSS is legal and Biome does not know it, so
        // every stylesheet using it reports an unknown function without this.
        "noUnknownFunction": {
          "level": "error",
          "options": { "ignore": ["theme"] }
        }
      },
      "a11y": {
        // tabIndex={0} on a scrollable region is the axe-mandated pattern
        // (scrollable-region-focusable), which this rule reads as a violation.
        "noNoninteractiveTabindex": "off"
      },
      "style": {
        // The Next app router names files `[slug]` and `(group)`, which no
        // case convention accepts.
        "useFilenamingConvention": "off",
        // Barrel re-exports are the module layout this codebase uses.
        "noExportedImports": "off"
      },
      "security": {
        // JSON-LD structured data has no route other than a static
        // dangerouslySetInnerHTML block. Keep the override narrow and review
        // every new use site by hand.
        "noDangerouslySetInnerHtml": "off"
      },
      "nursery": {
        // A test with no assertion passes whatever the code does. Nursery, so
        // it is off in every preset and cannot be enabled from overrides.
        "useExpect": "error"
      }
    }
  }
}
